r-widget-container"><h1><strong>Web hacking: understand how it works and le=
arn about the main types of cyberattacks.</strong></h1><p><span style=3D"fo=
nt-weight: 400;">According to data released by CNN, in 2022 </span><b>Brazi=
l was the second country in Latin America with the most cyberattacks.</b><s=
pan style=3D"font-weight: 400;">. </span></p><p><span style=3D"font-weight:=
 400;">Therefore, there is an increasing need for companies to have profess=
ionals like these. <strong>Web hacking experts are able to predict and prot=
ect their organizations from experiencing this situation.</strong></span></=
p><p><span style=3D"font-weight: 400;">In this text, we will explain what w=
eb hacking is and how it works, the main types of attacks a company is susc=
eptible to, and how ethical hacking can help organizations protect themselv=
es.</span></p><h2><strong>What is web hacking?</strong></h2><p><strong>Web =
hacking is a practice that aims to exploit vulnerabilities in web applicati=
ons to gain unauthorized access, manipulate data, or cause damage to the sy=
stem.</strong></p><p><strong>Malicious hackers, also known as <i>black hats=
</i>, They seek to compromise security.</strong><span style=3D"font-weight:=
 400;"><strong> of websites and systems to steal information, extort money,=
 or cause harm.</strong> </span></p><p><span style=3D"font-weight: 400;">Th=
eir main focus is </span><b>sensitive data</b><span style=3D"font-weight: 4=
00;">, such as user credentials, financial information, and intellectual pr=
operty.</span></p><p><span style=3D"font-weight: 400;">These attacks can be=
 carried out in various ways, such as:</span></p><ul><li style=3D"font-weig=
ht: 400;" aria-level=3D"1"><b>SQL Injection =E2=80=94 </b><span style=3D"fo=
nt-weight: 400;">Commands entered into input forms to manipulate databases;=
</span></li><li style=3D"font-weight: 400;" aria-level=3D"1"><b>Cross-site =
scripting (XSS) attacks =E2=80=94</b><span style=3D"font-weight: 400;"> mal=
icious scripts injected into web pages;</span></li><li style=3D"font-weight=
: 400;" aria-level=3D"1"><b>Exploiting authentication and authorization vul=
nerabilities</b><span style=3D"font-weight: 400;">.</span></li></ul><h2><sp=
an style=3D"font-weight: 400;">What are White Hats?</span></h2><p><span sty=
le=3D"font-weight: 400;">On the other hand, ethical hackers (or </span><i><=
span style=3D"font-weight: 400;">white hats</span></i><span style=3D"font-w=
eight: 400;">They use the same techniques, but with permission from the sys=
tem owners. </span></p><p><span style=3D"font-weight: 400;">Here, the goal =
of these professionals is </span><b>identify and correct faults </b><a href=
=3D"https://blog.eseg.edu.br/o-que-e-seguranca-digital/"><b>digital securit=
y</b></a><strong> before malicious hackers can exploit them.</strong></p><p=
><i><span style=3D"font-weight: 400;">White hats</span></i><span style=3D"f=
ont-weight: 400;"> They are hired to perform penetration testing and securi=
ty audits, helping to improve the resilience of web applications.</span></p=
><blockquote><p><b>Read also: </b><a href=3D"https://blog.eseg.edu.br/compu=
tacao-quantica-e-ciberseguranca/"><b>Quantum computing and the need for cyb=
ersecurity.</b></a></p></blockquote><h2><strong>What are the main types of =
cyberattacks?</strong></h2><p><span style=3D"font-weight: 400;">By understa=
nding the main hacking techniques used to infiltrate websites and applicati=
ons, we can understand some of the main cyberattacks and how each one works=
.</span></p><h3><strong>Phishing</strong></h3><p><span style=3D"font-weight=
: 400;">The focus of a phishing attack is </span><b>stealing confidential i=
nformation</b><span style=3D"font-weight: 400;">, <strong>such as passwords=
 and bank details, deceiving the user with fake emails and links.</strong> =
</span></p><p><span style=3D"font-weight: 400;">A classic example is the se=
nding of communications that impersonate financial institutions and induce =
the recipient to provide credentials.</span></p><h3><strong>Ransomware</str=
ong></h3><p><span style=3D"font-weight: 400;">In a cyberattack, Ransomware,=
 the criminals </span><b>They infect a system and encrypt its files.</b><sp=
an style=3D"font-weight: 400;">, requiring a payment, usually in cryptocurr=
ency, to unlock access.</span></p><h3><strong>Malware</strong></h3><p><span=
 style=3D"font-weight: 400;">This term is used to refer to any </span><b>ma=
licious software designed to harm the system.</b><span style=3D"font-weight=
: 400;">. It is capable of stealing data, damaging files, or allowing remot=
e control of devices.</span></p><h3><strong>DDoS (Distributed Denial of Ser=
vice Attack)</strong></h3><p><span style=3D"font-weight: 400;">In a DDoS at=
tack, <strong>multiple devices </strong></span><b>overload a server or netw=
ork</b><span style=3D"font-weight: 400;"> and make it unavailable to legiti=
mate users.</span></p><p><span style=3D"font-weight: 400;"> A well-known ex=
ample was the 2006 attack on Dyn, which took down major websites such as Tw=
itter and Netflix.</span></p><blockquote><p><b>Read more: </b><a href=3D"ht=
tps://blog.eseg.edu.br/saiba-mais-sobre-seguranca-digital-governanca-e-gest=
ao-de-dados/">Learn more about digital security, governance, and data manag=
ement.</a></p></blockquote><h2><strong>How does ethical hacking help protec=
t businesses?</strong></h2><p><span style=3D"font-weight: 400;">The best wa=
y for companies to protect themselves against cyberattacks is to invest in =
professionals in the field of ethical hacking.&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong>B=
y identifying weaknesses before criminals do, companies can correct flaws a=
nd prevent data breaches, service interruptions, and reputational damage.</=
strong></p><p><span style=3D"font-weight: 400;">Furthermore, these practice=
s help the organization to </span><b>to act in accordance with safety regul=
ations.</b><span style=3D"font-weight: 400;">, like the</span> <span style=
=3D"font-weight: 400;">LGPD</span><span style=3D"font-weight: 400;">, which=
 require the protection of sensitive customer and user information.</span><=
/p><p><strong>In practice, ethical hackers can use various techniques, such=
 as vulnerability scanning, network analysis, simulated attacks, and social=
 engineering to test the resilience of systems.</strong></p><p><span style=
=3D"font-weight: 400;">In this way, they are able to identify flaws, docume=
nt findings, and recommend corrections. </span></p><p><span style=3D"font-w=
eight: 400;">For example: <strong>By simulating an SQL injection attack, th=
e professional can demonstrate how sensitive data can be exposed and sugges=
t preventative measures.</strong> to protect the database used by the compa=
ny.</span></p><p><b>Read more: </b><a href=3D"https://blog.eseg.edu.br/o-qu=
e-e-sre/"><b>What is a Site Reliability Engineer (SRE)? Find out!</b></a></=
p><h2><strong>Why is a degree in Computer Engineering important for working=
 in cybersecurity?</strong></h2><p><span style=3D"font-weight: 400;">If you=
're interested in web hacking, you should know that... </span><a href=3D"ht=
tps://blog.eseg.edu.br/engenharia-da-computacao/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"=
noopener"><span style=3D"font-weight: 400;">Bachelor's degree in Computer E=
ngineering</span></a><span style=3D"font-weight: 400;"> It gives you more k=
nowledge to work in this area.</span></p><p><span style=3D"font-weight: 400=
;">This training provides a <strong>solid foundation in programming, networ=
king, operating systems, and computer architecture.,</strong> allowing prof=
essionals to understand deeply <strong>How computing software and hardware =
work</strong> and consequently, how to protect them from digital threats.</=
span></p><p><strong>Throughout the specialization, engineers learn to perfo=
rm penetration tests, simulate attacks such as SQL injection, cross-site sc=
ripting (XSS), and distributed denial-of-service (DDoS) attacks, and develo=
p defense solutions.</strong></p><p><span style=3D"font-weight: 400;">In ad=
dition, they also acquire </span><b>skills in cryptography, access control =
and </b><b>forensic analysis</b><span style=3D"font-weight: 400;">, essenti=
al for preventing and responding to security incidents.</span></p><p><span =
style=3D"font-weight: 400;">So, did you understand what web hacking is, wha=
t the main types of cyberattacks are, and how the field of ethical hacking =
helps a company stay protected and up-to-date?</span></p><p><em><strong>If =
